  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decode_R13_R2000",
    "file": "libredwg/src/decode.c",
    "description": "Root cause is missing bounds enforcement for the header-variables bitstream before calling dwg_decode_header_variables. decode_R13_R2000 reads dwg->header_vars.size (RL) but does not constrain Bit_Chain (dat->size/end) to that section length prior to parsing the many FIELD_B/... reads in header_variables.spec. As a result, bit_read_B in bits.c can be driven to dat->byte == dat->size and perform dat->chain[dat->byte] OOB read (CHK_OVERFLOW only rejects > size, not == size with bit==0).",
    "conditions": "In llvmfuzz, attacker-controlled DWG bytes set up a valid-enough R13/R2000 decode path and a malformed/truncated header variables section/length relationship. decode_R13_R2000 enters section 0, sets dat->byte to section start+16, reads header_vars.size, then dwg_decode_header_variables consumes fields past available input because no hard parse boundary is applied for that section. Eventually a FIELD_B read reaches end-of-buffer and triggers 1-byte heap OOB read in bit_read_B."
  },
